file_manager: folders that recursive file lists don't walk

server.files.list walks a root recursively, on the event loop, and costs
~14 ms per file on the AD5X (a resolve() and the reserved path checks
for each one). Mainsail and Fluidd ask for the config root at each page
load. Since v0.1.0-rc1 the config folder holds the "plugins" link to
/data/ad5x/plugins (kiln_os.link_plugins), so the listing walks every
installed plugin too: with kiln-notify and afc-kiln (~2200 files) each
page load blocked Moonraker for about a minute (EVENT LOOP BLOCKED 56-58
s), the web UIs stopped loading and the Klippy connection dropped.

add_unlisted_path() marks a folder that get_file_list() doesn't enter.
Clients still browse it with get_directory, and its files can be read,
edited and uploaded as before; they are only missing from the flat
config list. kiln_os registers the plugins folder once it is linked.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)

diff --git a/moonraker/components/file_manager/file_manager.py b/moonraker/components/file_manager/file_manager.py
--- a/moonraker/components/file_manager/file_manager.py
+++ b/moonraker/components/file_manager/file_manager.py
@@ -69,6 +69,9 @@
         self.server = config.get_server()
         self.event_loop = self.server.get_event_loop()
         self.reserved_paths: Dict[str, Tuple[pathlib.Path, bool]] = {}
+        # Kiln OS: folders clients can browse that recursive file lists
+        # (server.files.list) don't walk (add_unlisted_path)
+        self.unlisted_paths: Set[pathlib.Path] = set()
         self.full_access_roots: Set[str] = set()
         self.file_paths: Dict[str, str] = {}
         app_args = self.server.get_app_args()
@@ -349,6 +352,17 @@
                 )
         return False
 
+    def add_unlisted_path(self, path: StrOrPath) -> None:
+        """Kiln OS: a folder (or a link to one) inside a root that
+        get_file_list() doesn't walk into. It stays browsable with
+        get_directory and its files stay readable and writable as before.
+        For big trees under a root, such as the plugins folder linked into
+        config: each file costs a resolve() and the reserved path checks,
+        and the listing runs on the event loop."""
+        if isinstance(path, str):
+            path = pathlib.Path(path)
+        self.unlisted_paths.add(path.expanduser().resolve())
+
     def add_reserved_path(
         self, name: str, res_path: StrOrPath, read_access: bool = True
     ) -> bool:
